<title>USA: US govt mediator suspends UPS pilot talks.</title>
<headline>US govt mediator suspends UPS pilot talks.</headline>
<dateline>LOUISVILLE 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. government mediator has suspended contract talks between UPS and its 1,900 pilots for three months, a company official said.</p>
<p>Talks reconvened in Washington DC last month, but failed to produce much progress, the official said.</p>
<p>The courier and the independent association representing UPS pilots have been negotiating new contract terms since 1995.</p>
<p>The unresolved issues all relate to compensation - including pay scales and retirement benefits. -- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+5017</p>
